# Build output
build/
build-cpm/
build-debug/
build-asan/
build-vulkan*/
compile_commands.json
# Runtime logs. Ogre writes ogre.log beside the working directory; the editor
# writes its playtest capture under artifacts/ with the other generated files.
ogre.log
artifacts/
.agents/
.codex/
.claude/
.opencode/
.goose/

# Pipeline source art living alongside the content packs: archives and DCC
# files are *inputs* to the asset pipeline, not build inputs -- what the game
# loads is the extracted mesh/texture committed under assets/<pack>/. 110 MB of
# these archives once lived in history and made a fresh clone ~800 MB, so they
# are ignored by extension wherever they land. The rules are extension-scoped
# on purpose: the packs hold .png/.obj/.toml/.material/.frag and are never
# touched by them.
assets/**/*.zip
assets/**/*.rar
assets/**/*.7z
assets/**/*.blend
assets/**/*.blend1
assets/**/*.fbx
assets/*.webm
# Screen captures are local scratch; the two the README embeds are committed.
assets/*.mp4
assets/*.gif
!assets/preview.mp4
!assets/preview.gif
docs/superpowers/

# Vendored SDK
vendor/ogre/

# Caches / editor-local state
.cache/
imgui.ini
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Periodic backups the editor writes beside a scene. Recovery material for one
# machine; the scene itself is the committed artefact.
*.autosave.scn
